    {
      "id": "e580ae4caf9c8932834b82b5e1b0f7020af4f114",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3691891705,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Yeah, that's not it. The problem is the `cppcheck.sh` script sends stderr to stdout as well, so errors get mixed up. We don't want to do that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-08-16T21:11:03.837Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-08-16T21:11:03.837Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 519892853,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 26190,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6c4f48bc9e565e12c2f51e920eb6bd42358ec5bf",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3692134560,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Actually, even worse, the results we want are written to `stderr` by default (they're considered errors in files, I guess), what's written to `stdout` are \"errors\" like \"all the files were excluded\".\n\nThere's an `--output-file` option, which then wouldn't print the errors in the log. We'd still want to display it if there were errors, though.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
